WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:04.060
The train on track 1 is now approaching.{let's go with the mbta phrasing to stay true to our uh, roots}{that's what I wanted to do}

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.370
I-I'm so sorry!

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.970
<i>My dream is to join S4!{or "join S4" but not "enter S4"}</i>

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:39.760
What's wrong?

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:41.770
You're not going to write it?

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.230
Yume-chan!

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.350
You talked about it so much, Koharu-chan.{please note that I don't let "always + progressive form" slip by very often}

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.270
Yeah, but still...

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.530
We'll do it together!

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.030
Huh?

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.530
Let's get into S4!

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.660
Koharu-chan!

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:04.580
Yume-chan!

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.750
Sorry I'm late.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.090
Everything okay?

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.590
Yep, since I made it!

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:16.890
Let's hurry inside.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:17.680
Sure!

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.600
Thank you!

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:29.610
They're fantastic!

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:52.830
Koharu-chan, that uniform is so becoming on you. {is this a thing?}{usually it's "that uniform really makes you"}{becoming of you?}

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.080
Same to you.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.590
Really? Aw, shucks.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.630
I wonder if we'll get to meet S4.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.720
That's right.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:05.640
Starting today, I'm a student at S4's school, Four Star Academy. {this?}{sounds good, unless you want to go fancy with something like uh, "quincestar academy"}

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.220
I'm so happy I've got the jitters!

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:27.120
Students, allow me to congratulate you on your matriculation.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.540
I am Moroboshi, headmaster of Four Star Academy. {I guess you're right, unlike Ichigo's va}

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:35.380
First I shall introduce your upperclassmen who represent a goal for you to strive toward.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:40.880
They are our school's top stars, the four ladies of S4.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:56.560
Whether you are able to become radiant idols as they are{how proud I am of you for not adding "or not"}

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.280
depends entirely upon your efforts that begin today.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.320
Yes!

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.400
Please introduce yourselves, S4.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:08.160
I'm Kasumi Yozora, from the Moon Beauty Class.{I'm going to un-reverse the class names because then you can see it's"beauty class", "theater class", etc. | also I like it better this way}

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.750
You've stepped into a harsh world, 
but we can get through this together.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:19.380
From the Wind Dance Class, it's Nikaidou Yuzu! {we can definitely get crazier like with Zephyr, though who knows what's coming}{Nikaidō is fine too if you want to go that route, and isn't it 伊達の舞}

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:25.260
Hear ye! I pledge to support you with all I've got as someone just a few steps ahead!{help, I can't tell if it's senpai or tensai}{don't be a silly}

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:31.060
I am Kisaragi Tsubasa, in the Bird Theater Class.{we could consider spelling it theatre to match http://www.birdtheatre.org/ (also, apparently 取り has a special meaning in theatre that should be TL-noted)}

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:36.520
I'll whip you all into shape with love, so look forward to it. {just whip my shit up, neo-ichigo}

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.610
From the Flower Song Class, Shiratori Hime.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:50.410
Should you ever stumble and lose your way as an idol, please seek out S4.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:57.790
As the brightest stars in the sky, we will serve as a beacon of light to help you get back on track.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:01.920
Congratulations on entering our academy.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:12.060
Aw man, we ended up in different classes, Koharu-chan.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:15.980
At least we're roommates, so we'll see each other all the time.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.190
I guess you're right. Well, my stop's here.{oh, nice}

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.310
Sure.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.070
Morning, babies.{I miss Johnny already}

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:39.080
I'm your class's homeroom teacher.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.340
Hibiki Anna!

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:47.340
You can bet I'll be rocking this year with you, so don't you forget it!{dat /ɹ/}

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:49.840
Say, girls.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:54.850
There's one important thing you must remember if you want to be the brightest star.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:56.980
What do you think it is?

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:00.480
Put simply...

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:02.480
It's individuality! {jesus the one time an english word has a million more syllables}

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.230
Individuality...

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:07.990
To foster your own personal glimmer at this academy,

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.490
we teach you how to self-produce.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:12.990
Self-produce...

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:18.200
That said, it's about time to pass out the rockingest item you'll need, so come when I call you.{if winningest can be a word, so can rockingest, right?}{it is now. you have only yourself to blame}

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.870
First, Aoyama Chiharu.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:21.170
Here.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:23.590
Let's see here... Nijino Yume.

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:24.750
Here!

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:29.510
This is your student ID, and here's your Aikatsu Mobile.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:36.260
Stop by the Dress Make Room later to pick out your School Dress. {it actually says Dress Make Room in english later on}{it's fine either way, though by the way, we should standardize our use of capital letters for proper aikatsu nouns for stars}{I'll keep a list this time}

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:38.270
Okay!

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.770
Next, Nonomiya Saki.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:42.060
Here.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:46.270
They're beautiful! I can hardly contain my excitement!

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:49.490
My Aikatsu's really going to start!

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:53.070
Next, Kaiyama Umi.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:54.240
Here.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:57.540
Like I said, my Aikatsu's really going...

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.540
Okutani Hanako.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:01.500
Here.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:11.800
You're a lifesaver. Thanks.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.720
Next... Sakuma Rena.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:15.300
It totes felt like I blew it on my first day.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:13.510
Here.

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.060
Hey, what's your name?

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:23.060
Um... it's Nijino Yume.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:25.520
Nice to meet'cha. I'm—

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:26.860
Sakuraba Rola. {ugh. yes? the site actually does say "Rola"}{yes}

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:27.820
Here.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:31.320
Not many people come in late on their first day.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:33.820
You must think highly of yourself.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:36.070
I'm sorry.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.080
Well, you could also say...

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.500
This is individuality!

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:46.080
Okay, baby. I'll let you off the hook this time.{I assume we're going to treat baby like honey}{apparently not!}

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.840
But don't expect another second chance.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.760
Just take these and go.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:01.220
All right girls, back to your seats.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:07.230
And with that, you're free to go.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:09.360
You can do whatever you'd like now, babies.

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:16.110
Think about how to make the most of your time. That's self-producing.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:17.620
Right then, bye-bee.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.370
What?

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:24.870
I heard some girls say they were going to train, and some others are going back to their rooms.

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:28.630
Wanna come explore the campus with me then?

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:33.380
Sure. Oh, my teacher told us there was a guide for new students. {no, she pulls it out. at the very least not 'they had'}

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:37.140
There's an app for it on the Aikatsu Mobiles.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:40.680
Greetings to all the new students.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.140
We'll show you all around the school.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.440
S4's gonna give us a guided tour! {had "the rundown" originally}

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.150
Let's start here!

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:51.650
Welcome to the cafeteria!

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:56.650
This is where we all come to do lunch and have a spot of girls talk.{quite, quite}{spot of? I don't recall writing that}

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.530
These are the Four Star Dorms.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:03.330
It's where the students of our academy live.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:07.540
Here is the Dress Make Room.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.880
You'll be able to customize your dresses here.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.050
New students?

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:14.050
Yes.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:16.050
Please come this way.

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:20.050
This is where you'll be creating your own cards.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:24.810
First, authenticate yourself using your student ID.
Then select "School Dress".

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:28.310
All you need to do is pick your favorite styles and colors.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.570
They're all so cute it's hard to choose.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.320
Finished!

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:41.320
Me too!

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.330
Here you are, Nijino Yume-san.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.580
Thank you!

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:54.460
I can't believe I have such a lovely dress that's all my own!

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.920
It feels like I'm already an idol! {yes, this is accurate. they're in fact not idols yet. hell, they haven't even called this an idol gakkou}

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.720
You're getting ahead of yourself, Yume-chan.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.550
I heard it's S4!

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:00.550
Let's go!

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:01.840
They said S4!

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:02.850
Let's check it out.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:06.350
It looks like they're leaving to record for a music show.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:09.850
They're so cool!

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.810
Their presence is on a different level.

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:14.440
Of course, they're each the top stars of their class!

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:20.110
And the one who was selected to represent the top of the Song Class was Shiratori Hime-san! {post capitalization}

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:25.410
They're even considered top-class among all the celebrities out there.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:30.410
I can't help but admire how incredible they all are.

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:34.790
Have a fine day. {I don't couldn't it's so late}

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:40.760
Huh? Yume-chan?

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:45.510
I'm gonna sneak ahead and see Hime-sama off!{I don't think you're using "head them off" correctly}{I thought I was. since when was that the real definition?}

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:48.980
Hime-sama!

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:51.520
What the... she's gone!

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:52.520
Gone!

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:53.770
Gone!

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:55.770
But why?!

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:57.940
No way!

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:57.940
Hey, you!

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:01.530
Who's that?

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:05.530
Seriously, what are you thinking climbing a tree in those clothes?

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:07.200
There's more than a few problems with it.

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.290
E-Excuse me?!

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:20.090
Huh?

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.050
Would you mind shoving off?

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.760
You're heavy.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:31.060
S-Sorry about that.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:43.490
I-I'm really sorry!

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.570
What were you even doing all the way up here?

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:52.330
More importantly, what are <i>you</i> doing here?{this is a nice font but the italics look weird}{they actually look good alone, but not at the same time. it's fine}

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:56.630
You're on the school grounds of Four Star Academy.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:59.090
Outsiders aren't allowed inside.

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:02.340
Huh? What, you new here?

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:07.090
So what if I am? If you don't scram, 
I'll call security on you.

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:09.350
Please, feel free.

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:11.350
We're in the boys section of the school right now. {branch? department? school?}{division is fine, but I'm calling the physical part of the school the boys section if you mindn't}

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:12.100
Huh?

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:15.850
If I had to say, you're the outsider here.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:22.110
Every year there's at least one who doesn't know about the boys division.

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:25.360
S-Sorry, I...

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:28.200
Just so you know, the girls are over that way.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:31.370
If you don't scram, I'll call security on you.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:35.870
You look like a boiled octopus!

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.380
Sorry for all the trouble!

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:47.760
You had me worried, disappearing like that.

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:51.720
My head was so full of S4 I got lost.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.770
You've always had no sense of direction, Yume-chan.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:59.520
Now then, looks like our lessons finally start tomorrow.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:02.780
After we learn our foundations as trainees, {here we go again. officially research students, and in akb it was understudies. I think this one works here}{I think, this better is}

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:05.030
we can take the class sorting audition. {this will be named something}

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:06.780
I see.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.290
Okay, one more time.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:19.920
That's enough.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:24.090
Nijino, you're terrible. You need to strengthen your abs.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:25.670
Right.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.510
Next, Sakuraba.

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:32.930
That's pretty darn good.

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.330
Yume-chan.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.250
How'd your first lessons go?

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:01.170
Just awful. Everyone else is so good already.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:04.130
But you're so good at singing, Yume-chan. {too many goods but I think it's ok}

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:07.920
The teacher said even that wasn't good enough.{she's talking about her sensei as a teacher, not as a person}

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:11.180
Still, I like your singing, Yume-chan.

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:15.680
Your songs always make me feel warm somehow.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:17.180
Do they?

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:22.190
I just look up to Hime-sama, and I love to sing.

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:26.440
Don't you think that's the most important thing?

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:29.450
Attention, girls.

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:34.330
All the trainees need to change into their uniforms and gather in the concert hall. {I wish hall was less ambiguous}

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:35.950
Is something happening?

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:40.790
You may not be ready, but we decided to go ahead with the trainee debut concert.

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:42.210
Get on it!

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:49.220
Good, you're all here for your debut concert.

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:55.720
This is your chance to strut your stuff in front of S4, 
your upperclassmen, and all the teachers.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:58.720
Baby, put your game face on!

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:01.230
What should I do?

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:04.190
Yume-chan, I'm so nervous!

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:05.980
You'll do great, Koharu-chan.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:10.240
Up next, Nanakura Koharu. Come on!

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.200
C-Coming.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.410
Break a leg!

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:15.570
Sure, I'll do my best.

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:16.620
Good luck!

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:26.880
Next, Nijino Yume.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.000
Here!

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:33.300
<i>S4 is going to watch me perform.</i>

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:36.640
<i>This is my very first time on stage.</i>

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:40.810
<i>My dream is to join S4.</i>

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:43.440
<i>I want to shine like S4!</i>

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:47.270
<i>I won't ever give up.</i>

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:49.070
<i>Not until I fulfill my dream.</i>

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:52.280
<i>It all begins here!</i>

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:13.190
That girl... is she really a first-year?

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:17.190
I know, she's well above your typical newcomer.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:19.690
We've got a live one on our hands!

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:23.070
Nijino Yume-chan.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:26.700
The tale of legends...{I think this might eventually make it into my "gripes about general translation patterns" list}

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:28.700
...begins anew.{honestly I just want to say "it's happening", thus this line}{the "again" is implied in english by the "new", but more importantly, I don't want you to say "it's happening"}

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:40.340
Yume-chan!

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:41.720
Yume-chan!

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:42.840
Nijino!

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:53.940
Where...

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.400
The infirmary.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:57.860
You're all right now.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.400
H-H-Hime-san?!

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:04.030
You did well.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:11.410
What's the matter?

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:17.000
Because... I've admired you forever, 
and now you're right in front of me... {not this time}

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:20.800
Don't cry, Yume-chan.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:25.430
Why... do you know my name?

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:29.930
I'll go let them know you've woken up. {or nurse if we're feeling like that. I wonder if we'll be seeing this room a lot}

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:32.850
Rest here for a bit longer.

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:34.020
Okay.

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:34.940
Yume-chan!

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:38.440
Are you okay, Yume-chan?

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:40.820
Sorry for scaring you. {and hey, she's still in her coord}

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:43.690
But don't worry! I'm in tip-top shape!

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:45.700
That's a relief.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:48.700
Your performance was really amazing!

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:51.200
You don't remember?

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:53.120
Hang on a second.

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:56.210
Um... there! Here, look.

00:21:57.420 --> 00:22:00.340
This is... me?

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:01.210
Yeah!

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:05.970
It's like you were a totally different person.

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:08.390
You were so awesome!

00:22:08.390 --> 00:22:13.930
Even the upperclassmen couldn't believe you had just started.

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:17.480
<i>I can't remember a thing.</i>

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:18.940
<i>How...</i>

00:22:20.810 --> 00:22:22.520
<i>Just what happened?</i>

00:23:57.950 --> 00:24:02.460
In this segment, S4 will present the hottest Aikatsu news.

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:06.170
Charming new students have just matriculated.

